Spec: Feature SQLite Concurrency & Indexer Synchronization (1.3 / STAB-04)

Purpose:
  Prevent SQLITE_BUSY errors, journal mode conflicts, and shutdown race conditions between DatabaseManager (GUI thread) and ImageIndexer (worker thread).

Platform: C++26 (Linux) / C++23 (Windows, macOS), Qt6

References:
  ../../../desktop-gallery.sdd

Owns:
  ./**

Can modify:
  /include/ImageIndexer.hpp
  /src/ImageIndexer.cpp
  /include/MainWindow.hpp
  /src/MainWindow.cpp
  /data/Prioritaetenliste.md

Must:
  Preserve the SQLite WAL journal mode configured in DatabaseManager::init() instead of overriding it with PRAGMA journal_mode = MEMORY in ImageIndexer::run().
  Configure PRAGMA busy_timeout = 5000 on the ImageIndexer database connection to handle concurrent access gracefully.
  Provide a thread-safe atomic cancellation mechanism (ImageIndexer::cancel()) and ensure MainWindow cancels any active indexer when starting a new scan or shutting down.

Must not:
  Switch SQLite journal_mode to MEMORY on a shared database connection.
  Leave running ImageIndexer tasks uncancelled when MainWindow is destroyed.

Tasks:
  [x] #1 Add atomic cancellation support to include/ImageIndexer.hpp and update SQLite pragmas and loop check in src/ImageIndexer.cpp.
  [x] #2 Track active ImageIndexer in MainWindow and ensure clean cancellation on re-scan and application exit.
  [x] #3 Verify compilation via cmake --build build and mark item 1.3 as completed in data/Prioritaetenliste.md.

Done when:
  cmake --build build succeeds without errors and ImageIndexer operates in WAL mode with busy_timeout and clean cancellation lifecycle.
